03 — SCIENTIFIC SIMULATION INTEGRITY
================================================================

This requirement is mandatory.

Explicitly distinguish three levels:

LEVEL A — SCIENTIFICALLY VALIDATED MODEL

A mathematical or computational physiological
model with documented assumptions, parameters,
source references, limitations, and validation
evidence appropriate to its intended use.

LEVEL B — SCIENTIFICALLY INFORMED EDUCATIONAL MODEL

A simplified educational representation of
a physiological process with explained
assumptions and scientifically supported
relationships, but not clinically validated
for individual prediction.

LEVEL C — ILLUSTRATIVE ANIMATION

A visual teaching aid showing the direction,
sequence, or general behavior of a process.

Do not label Level B or Level C as validated
medical simulations.

Do not imply that visual realism proves
scientific or physiological accuracy.

Do not invent:

- Hemodynamic measurements
- Oxygen saturation predictions
- Patient-specific ECG signals
- Blood pressure relationships
- Drug concentrations
- Clinical diagnostic conclusions
- Anatomical structures
- Physiological equations

Every numerical model must document
its equations, units, assumptions,
valid parameter ranges, and limitations.

Clearly label illustrative values.

The application is for education,
not medical diagnosis or patient management.

